# palm-init mounts what is listed here at boot, once it has mounted /proc
# /sys /dev /dev/pts /dev/shm /run /tmp itself (lines for those are skipped).
# It checks and remounts `/` from its line, then mounts the rest in order and
# turns on swap lines (distro/init/fstab.odin). The disk image adds `/` and
# the EFI system partition by label; the installer adds them by PARTUUID.
#
# Devices: /dev/..., UUID=, LABEL=, PARTUUID=, PARTLABEL=. A pass of 1 or 2
# runs fsck.<type> -p first, when one is installed.
#
# <device>  <mountpoint>  <type>  <options>  <dump>  <pass>
